  "familyDescriptions": {
    "felidae": "The cat family - obligate carnivores built around retractable claws, acute night vision, and a stalk-and-ambush hunting style, ranging from the domestic cat to the tiger, the largest living cat.",
    "ursidae": "Bears - large, plantigrade omnivores found on every continent but Africa and Australia, united by a stocky build, small eyes, and (in most species) a period of winter dormancy."
  }
